usage: test.py [-h] [--checkpoint CHECKPOINT] [--save_dir SAVE_DIR]
               [--pkl_save_dir PKL_SAVE_DIR]
               [--pr_curve_save_dir PR_CURVE_SAVE_DIR]
               [--output_detsample_dir OUTPUT_DETSAMPLE_DIR] [--metric METRIC]
               [--work-dir WORK_DIR] [--ceph] [--show] [--show-dir SHOW_DIR]
               [--score-thr SCORE_THR]
               [--task {mono_det,multi-view_det,lidar_det,lidar_seg,multi-modality_det}]
               [--wait-time WAIT_TIME]
               [--cfg-options CFG_OPTIONS [CFG_OPTIONS ...]]
               [--launcher {none,pytorch,slurm,mpi}] [--tta]
               [--local_rank LOCAL_RANK]
               config

MMDet3D test (and eval) a model

positional arguments:
  config                test config file path

optional arguments:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --checkpoint CHECKPOINT
                        checkpoint file
  --save_dir SAVE_DIR   save detection results
  --pkl_save_dir PKL_SAVE_DIR
                        save pickle file
  --pr_curve_save_dir PR_CURVE_SAVE_DIR
                        save PR curve
  --output_detsample_dir OUTPUT_DETSAMPLE_DIR
                        output_detsample_dir
  --metric METRIC       metric
  --work-dir WORK_DIR   the directory to save the file containing evaluation
                        metrics
  --ceph                Use ceph as data storage backend
  --show                show prediction results
  --show-dir SHOW_DIR   directory where painted images will be saved. If
                        specified, it will be automatically saved to the
                        work_dir/timestamp/show_dir
  --score-thr SCORE_THR
                        bbox score threshold
  --task {mono_det,multi-view_det,lidar_det,lidar_seg,multi-modality_det}
                        Determine the visualization method depending on the
                        task.
  --wait-time WAIT_TIME
                        the interval of show (s)
  --cfg-options CFG_OPTIONS [CFG_OPTIONS ...]
                        override some settings in the used config, the key-
                        value pair in xxx=yyy format will be merged into
                        config file. If the value to be overwritten is a list,
                        it should be like key="[a,b]" or key=a,b It also
                        allows nested list/tuple values, e.g.
                        key="[(a,b),(c,d)]" Note that the quotation marks are
                        necessary and that no white space is allowed.
  --launcher {none,pytorch,slurm,mpi}
                        job launcher
  --tta                 Test time augmentation
  --local_rank LOCAL_RANK, --local-rank LOCAL_RANK
